      <failure message="PaymentGateway.Exceptions.PaymentException was not thrown. The Stripe adapter accepted a charge request for a card that expired in 01/2023 without raising an exception. Expected behaviour: when the card expiry date is in the past relative to the transaction timestamp, the adapter must throw PaymentException with ErrorCode=CardExpired before transmitting the authorisation request to the Stripe API. This ensures that we do not incur Stripe processing fees for transactions that are guaranteed to be declined. The card details used in this test: token=tok_visa_chargeDeclinedExpiredCard, amount=99.99 GBP, currency=GBP, customer_id=cus_test_expired_001. Stack trace follows: at PaymentGateway.Adapters.StripeAdapter.ChargeAsync(ChargeRequest request) in StripeAdapter.cs:line 47, at PaymentGateway.Tests.StripeAdapterTests.ChargeCard_ExpiredCard_ThrowsPaymentException() in StripeAdapterTests.cs:line 88. Assertion: Assert.Throws&lt;PaymentException&gt;() — no exception was thrown. Additional context: the ExpiryValidator.IsExpired() helper returns True for this card but the guard clause on line 44 of StripeAdapter.cs was removed in commit a3f91bc without a corresponding test update." />
    </testcase>

